# CRUD security

## Plugin semantics

CRUD accelerates HTTP actions; it does **not** relax mass assignment, serialization, or authorization. RelatedModels / patchable associations are common overexposure vectors.

## Required behavior

- Keep Entity `_accessible` tight — especially `role`, auth flags, and association patches.
- Hide secrets via `$_hidden` / API shaping even when Api listeners serialize entities.
- Authorize/scoped-load resources on view/edit/delete (IDOR) — “CRUD found it” is not permission.
- Treat RelatedModels config as a security surface; only expose associations intentionally.
- When Authorization is installed, prefer policy/scope patterns (see CRUD+AuthZ integration).

## Anti-patterns

- mass-assignment-overexposure via CRUD patch
- serialization-overexposure on Api listeners
- IDOR on CRUD view/edit by primary key alone
- Wide RelatedModels “for convenience”
